  "pending_reason": "The frozen positive-radius, non-strict success-event statement and the formal root have the same regression model, critical inequality, constants and conclusion. The additional boundedness/integrability hypotheses follow from finite-dimensional localization. Sphere nonemptiness is not automatic, but its missing case has a direct star-scaling reduction yielding a stronger pointwise error bound. Splitting on that sphere and applying the root only in the nonempty case recovers the entire frozen statement; conversely the frozen statement immediately specializes to the root's hypotheses.",
